-- Q3736: Privacy Requirements and Data Protection [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per 45 CFR 164.308(a)(1)(ii)(A) and NIST SP 800-66 Rev. 2, covered entities must conduct a thorough assessment of potential risks and vulnerabilities to the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of electronic protected health information (ePHI). This risk analysis is the foundation of the HIPAA security management process and drives the selection of appropriate safeguards.
Wrong (A): The risk analysis focuses on identifying threats to ePHI, not calculating financial costs of breaches for insurance purposes.
Wrong (B): The risk analysis assesses vulnerabilities to ePHI, not which employees should have blanket access to all patient records.
