Wrong (A): A sole proprietor with only $15,000 in annual revenue that does not buy or sell personal information meets none of the CCPA/CPRA thresholds.
Wrong (C): The CCPA/CPRA explicitly excludes nonprofit organizations from its requirements, regardless of data processing volume.
