-- Q3741: Privacy Requirements and Data Protection [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per NIST SP 800-122 and AICPA Trust Services Criteria P1.0 (Privacy), a privacy impact assessment evaluates how a system collects, uses, shares, and maintains personal information. The primary focus is identifying privacy risks and assessing whether processing is proportionate to its stated legitimate aim, ensuring compliance with applicable regulations.
Wrong (A): Evaluating return on investment is a business decision, not a privacy concern. A PIA focuses on data protection risks, not financial metrics.
Wrong (C): Total cost of ownership is a procurement and budgeting consideration unrelated to identifying privacy risks in data processing.
Wrong (D): A vendor''s market share has no bearing on the privacy risks posed by the monitoring system to employees'' personal data.$EXPL$
