-- Q3749: SOC Engagements [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AICPA SSAE 18 (AT-C Section 320), a SOC 2 report is a restricted-use report intended only for management of the service organization, user entities, business partners, and prospective user entities with sufficient knowledge of the system. The detailed control descriptions and test results require adequate context to interpret.
Wrong (A): SOC 2 is not a general-use report. That description applies to a SOC 3 report, which omits detailed test results and may be freely distributed.
Wrong (B): The report is not limited solely to the service organization''s management. User entities and their auditors are also intended recipients.
Wrong (C): SOC 2 reports are not filed with the SEC. They are private restricted-use reports distributed directly to authorized parties.$EXPL$
