-- Q3750: SOC Engagements [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AICPA SSAE 18 (AT-C Section 320), a SOC 3 report is a general-use report that contains the service auditor''s opinion but omits detailed descriptions of tests and results. It can be freely distributed and displayed publicly, such as a SOC 3 seal on a website.
Wrong (B): A SOC 3 report contains less detail than a SOC 2 report, not more. It omits the detailed testing information that SOC 2 reports include.
Wrong (C): SOC 3 reports evaluate controls against the Trust Services Criteria, not controls relevant to ICFR. ICFR is the focus of SOC 1 engagements.
Wrong (D): SOC 3 reports can be issued for both Type I and Type II engagements. There is no restriction limiting SOC 3 to Type II only.$EXPL$
