-- Q3751: SOC Engagements [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AICPA SSAE 18 (AT-C Section 320), a SOC Type I engagement evaluates the suitability of the design of controls at a specific point in time (as of a specified date), assessing whether controls are suitably designed to meet applicable criteria. It does not test operating effectiveness.
Wrong (A): Testing operating effectiveness over a specified period is the focus of a Type II engagement, not a Type I engagement.
Wrong (B): Evaluating both design and operating effectiveness over a period describes a Type II engagement, which goes beyond the point-in-time scope of Type I.
Wrong (C): SOC engagements evaluate controls at a service organization, not the organization''s financial statements. Financial statement audits are governed by AU-C standards.$EXPL$
