Wrong (A): A SOC 1 Type I report evaluates only control design at a single point in time, not operating effectiveness over a period. It would not address whether controls operated effectively throughout the audit period.
Wrong (B): A SOC 2 Type I report evaluates Trust Services Criteria controls at a point in time, not ICFR-relevant controls over a period.
