  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SSAE 18 (AT-C Section 320), scoping a SOC engagement requires defining the system boundaries — the infrastructure, software, people, procedures, and data that support the services provided to user entities. The system description must clearly delineate what is included in and excluded from the examination scope.
Wrong (B): Employee headcount is an organizational metric, not a system boundary component. Scoping focuses on the system components directly supporting service delivery.
Wrong (C): Annual revenue is a financial metric irrelevant to defining the system boundaries for a SOC engagement.
Wrong (D): The geographic location of headquarters does not determine system scope. Controls at distributed locations may be in scope regardless of headquarters location.$EXPL$
