-- Q3755: SOC Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SSAE 18 (AT-C Section 320.14), when a service organization uses a subservice organization, two approaches are available: the inclusive method (subservice controls are included in scope and tested) or the carve-out method (subservice controls are excluded but identified in the system description). The choice depends on engagement circumstances.
Wrong (B): The service organization is not required to always include subservice controls. The carve-out method is a legitimate alternative that excludes them from the examination scope.
Wrong (C): There is no requirement that the subservice organization obtain its own separate SOC report before the primary engagement can proceed.
Wrong (D): The service auditor does not always directly test subservice controls. Under the carve-out method, subservice controls are excluded from the examination scope.$EXPL$
