-- Q3765: SOC Engagements [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per SSAE 18 (AT-C Section 320.56), the gap between the examination period end date (December 31) and report issuance (March 15) creates a risk that controls may have changed or new issues may have arisen during the interval. The service auditor''s opinion covers only the stated examination period, leaving events after period-end unexamined.
Wrong (A): The opinion covers only the examination period. Events occurring after December 31 are not examined and could materially affect the control environment.
Wrong (B): There is no 30-day issuance deadline that would invalidate the report. The concern is the coverage gap, not the report''s validity.
Wrong (D): Bridge letters are optional tools user entities may request to address the gap. They are not mandatory, and the risk exists regardless of whether one is obtained.$EXPL$
