-- Q3769: SOC Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per AT-C Section 320.09, the scope of a SOC 1 engagement includes all services relevant to user entities'' internal control over financial reporting. Payroll processing, benefits administration, and tax filing all generate transactions flowing into user entities'' financial statements, so all three are in scope.
Wrong (A): Limiting scope to the highest-volume service alone is incorrect. AT-C 320 requires inclusion of every service that could affect user entities'' ICFR, regardless of relative volume.
Wrong (B): Tax filing alone does not define the scope. Regulatory compliance is one factor, but all services affecting financial reporting must be included.
Wrong (D): Benefits administration alone does not define scope. While it involves employee data, the scoping criterion is relevance to ICFR, not the type of data processed.$EXPL$
