-- Q3770: SOC Engagements [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per AT-C Section 320.20 and the AICPA SOC 1 Guide, the inclusive method requires the service auditor to include the subservice organization''s relevant controls within the examination scope. The auditor tests these controls and includes them in the system description, control objectives, and testing results.
Wrong (B): This describes the carve-out method, not the inclusive method. Under the carve-out approach, subservice controls are excluded from scope and identified in the system description.
Wrong (C): The inclusive method does not require the subservice organization to first obtain its own SOC report. The service auditor directly tests the subservice controls.
