-- Q3777: SOC Reporting and Trust Services Criteria [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under the AICPA Trust Services Criteria (TSC 2017, Section 100), the five valid categories are security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality, and privacy. Profitability is not a Trust Services category and must be removed from the SOC 2 engagement scope.
Wrong (A): Security is the foundational category required in all SOC 2 engagements. While it is mandatory, it is still a valid Trust Services criterion that belongs in the scope listing.
Wrong (B): Availability is a valid Trust Services criterion that can be included in SOC 2 scope. Uptime requirements in SLAs are separate from the availability controls evaluated in a SOC 2.
Wrong (D): Privacy is one of the five valid Trust Services Criteria and can be included in SOC 2 scope. While HIPAA also governs privacy, the AICPA framework independently addresses privacy controls.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3777;
